-- ============================================================
-- scja1: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024 -- THE SEAT LAYER for sections 1 to 29E.
-- The source is a plain-text rendering (a converter's output), not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who wishes to start, defend or appeal a civil case in the Singapore High Court or the Court of Appeal. This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported
-- above as the questions that person would ask: which court hears my case and how, which court has jurisdiction, may the hearing be in private or by video link, how many Judges sit, may I appeal
-- and do I need permission, may the Judge hear further arguments, and to which court does my appeal go. Nothing here is new law. There is no seat for an official: where a provision addresses only
-- an official (the ranking of Judges, the Chief Justice's powers of appointment, the President's power to vary a sum), the rule is in layer 1 and the person meets it only through the questions below.
--
-- NAMES. Every question begins "Under section N," with the Act's own numbering, and every helper begins "scja1 seat", so that no two parts of the merged seat layer can share a name.
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list), one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- The records and MAYBE inputs the layer-1 rules expect are built inside each question from those answers, and the SAME layer-1 rule is then called; no rule is restated here.
--   * A fact the person may not know, or that a Schedule (not in this part) decides, is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure"; "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING and a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * An amount that the person does not know is asked as 0 and becomes NOTHING (the Act does not say how a case with no amount in dispute counts).
--   * What the Rules of Court and the Family Justice Rules prescribe is not among the sources: the person says whether the Rules do so.
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT. JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act, as encoded here, does not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- Never read NOTHING as no. A question marked "NOT" in its wording (for example, whether an appeal CANNOT be brought) has JUST TRUE for the restriction.

DECLARE `scja1 seat answer` IS ONE OF
    `scja1 seat Yes`
    `scja1 seat No`
    `scja1 seat I am not sure`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs. Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `scja1 seat answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`scja1 seat what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `scja1 seat Yes` THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `scja1 seat No` THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `scja1 seat I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- An amount that the person gives as 0 when they do not know it.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`scja1 seat my amount if I know it` MEANS
    IF amount EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST amount -- input mapping

-- A date that the person gives only if the event has happened.
GIVEN happened IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`scja1 seat the date if it has happened` MEANS
    IF happened THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

-- A decision of a court in a civil proceeding, built from what the person knows. The subject and the order are not asked: no rule of sections 1 to 29E turns on them.
GIVEN `the court that made my decision` IS A Court
      `the jurisdiction the court exercised` IS A `Jurisdiction exercised`
      `my decision was made after a trial of an action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount in dispute, in dollars, or 0 if I do not know` IS A NUMBER
      `the date my decision was made` IS A DATE
      `the judgment or order has been extracted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the judgment or order was extracted` IS A DATE
      `a written law says my decision is final or that no appeal lies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Decision
`scja1 seat my decision from what I know` MEANS
    Decision OF `the court that made my decision`, `the jurisdiction the court exercised`, `a civil proceeding`, `any other civil matter`, (Order OF `another order or application`, `granted unconditionally`), `my decision was made after a trial of an action`, FALSE, (`scja1 seat my amount if I know it` `the amount in dispute, in dollars, or 0 if I do not know`), `the date my decision was made`, (`scja1 seat the date if it has happened` `the judgment or order has been extracted` `the date the judgment or order was extracted`), `a written law says my decision is final or that no appeal lies`, FALSE

-- A hearing of one part of a civil proceeding, with the facts the rules of hearings turn on.
GIVEN `how the hearing is conducted` IS A `Manner of hearing`
      `oral evidence is given in this part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Hearing
`scja1 seat my hearing from what I know` MEANS
    Hearing OF (Bench OF `General Division`, EMPTY), `how the hearing is conducted`, `a civil proceeding`, `oral evidence is given in this part`, `all the parties consent`, FALSE, (`Split of opinion` OF 0, 0)

-- A date that no rule in the question reads: it fills a field of the decision that the question's rule ignores.
`scja1 seat a date the rule ignores` MEANS Date 1 1 2000

§ `The Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Will my matter be heard in private? (s 8)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 8(2). The court may hear any matter or proceeding in private if it is satisfied it is expedient on one of the grounds listed. You say which ground and whether the court is satisfied.
@export Under section 8(2), can the court hear my matter or proceeding in private?
GIVEN `the ground the court relies on` IS A `s 8(2) ground` @desc On which ground might the court hear the matter in private: the interests of justice, public safety, public security, propriety, the national interest of Singapore, the national security of Singapore, or another sufficient reason?
      `the court is satisfied that it is expedient on that ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is expedient on that ground to hear the matter in private?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 8(2), can the court hear my matter in private` IS
    `s 8(2) the court has power to hear the matter or proceeding in private` (IF `the court is satisfied that it is expedient on that ground` THEN LIST `the ground the court relies on` ELSE EMPTY)

-- ss 8(2AA) and 8(2AB), gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B; fork F5).
@export Under sections 8(2AA) and 8(2AB), will my application to hold a matter in private on the ground of national interest or national security be heard in private?
GIVEN `my application is for a matter to be held in private on the ground of the national interest or national security of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application for a matter to be held in private on the ground of the national interest or national security of Singapore?
      `it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the application otherwise than in private` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the application, or the part, otherwise than in private?
      `it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national security to hear it otherwise than in private` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national security of Singapore to hear the application, or the part, otherwise than in private?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under sections 8(2AA) and 8(2AB), will my application be heard in private` IS
    `ss 8(2AA) and 8(2AB) the application will be heard in private` `my application is for a matter to be held in private on the ground of the national interest or national security of Singapore` `it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the application otherwise than in private` `it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national security to hear it otherwise than in private`

-- s 8(5). A court that hears a matter, or part of it, in private may in its discretion permit a journalist for a newspaper or broadcasting service, a person with a sufficient interest, or anyone else it specifies, to be present.
@export Under section 8(5), may the court let me be present while it hears the matter in private?
GIVEN `the kind of person I am` IS A `s 8(5) individual` @desc Are you a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service, a person the court determines has a sufficient interest in the matter, any other individual the court specifies, or another individual?
      `the court hears the whole or a part of the matter in private` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court hear the whole or a part of the matter in private?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 8(5), may the court let me be present in the courtroom` IS
    `s 8(5) the court may permit the individual to be present in the courtroom` `the kind of person I am` `the court hears the whole or a part of the matter in private`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Can my hearing be by video, television or audio link? (s 8A)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 8A(1). Without limiting section 8, the court may conduct the hearing of any matter or proceeding, other than a matter the Rules prescribe, through a live video link, a live television link, a live audio link or any other electronic means the Chief Justice approves.
@export Under section 8A(1), can the court conduct the hearing of my matter through this means?
GIVEN `the matter is one the rules prescribe as outside electronic hearings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules prescribe as outside electronic hearings?
      `how the hearing would be conducted` IS A `Manner of hearing` @desc How would the hearing be conducted: through a live video link, a live television link, a live audio link only, or another way?
      `another electronic means approved by the Chief Justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the hearing is to be by another electronic means, has the Chief Justice approved it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 8A(1), can the court conduct my hearing this way` IS
    `s 8A(1) the court may conduct the hearing of the matter through the means` `the matter is one the rules prescribe as outside electronic hearings` `how the hearing would be conducted` `another electronic means approved by the Chief Justice`

-- s 8A(3). A court must not conduct a part of a criminal hearing where oral evidence is given, or a part of a civil hearing where oral evidence is given and the parties do not all consent, through a live audio link only.
@export Under section 8A(3), must the court not conduct this part of my civil hearing through a live audio link only?
GIVEN `oral evidence is given in this part of the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is oral evidence given in this part of the hearing?
      `all the parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the parties consent to this part being conducted through a live audio link only?
      `the matter is one the rules prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Rules of Court, the Family Justice Rules or the Criminal Procedure Rules prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 8A(3), must the court not use an audio link only for this part` IS
    `s 8A(3) the court must not conduct this part of the hearing through a live audio link only` (`scja1 seat my hearing from what I know` `through a live audio link only` `oral evidence is given in this part of the hearing` `all the parties consent`) `the matter is one the rules prescribe`

-- s 8A(5). The court must not conduct the hearing the way section 8A(1) allows if that would be inconsistent with its duty to ensure the hearing is conducted fairly to all parties.
@export Under section 8A(5), must the court not conduct my hearing through a video, television or electronic link?
GIVEN `to conduct it this way would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the hearing is conducted fairly to all parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would conducting the hearing this way be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that it is conducted fairly to all parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 8A(5), must the court not conduct my hearing this way` IS
    `s 8A(5) the court must not conduct the hearing in the manner provided under section 8A(1)` `to conduct it this way would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the hearing is conducted fairly to all parties`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Who sits on my case, and when? (ss 10 to 14)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 10(1). Every proceeding in the General Division is heard before a single Judge, or before any other number of Judges as a written law provides.
@export Under section 10(1), before how many Judges will my proceeding in the General Division be heard?
GIVEN `the number of Judges a written law provides for my proceeding, or 0 if none does` IS A NUMBER @desc If a written law provides that your proceeding is heard before a number of Judges other than one, how many? (0 if none does)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 10(1), before how many Judges will my proceeding be heard` IS
    `s 10(1) the number of Judges before whom the proceeding is heard and disposed of` (`scja1 seat my amount if I know it` `the number of Judges a written law provides for my proceeding, or 0 if none does`)

-- s 10(1A). The Chief Justice may direct that a proceeding be heard before any uneven number of Judges greater than the number under section 10(1).
@export Under section 10(1A), may the Chief Justice direct that my proceeding be heard before this number of Judges?
GIVEN `the number of Judges directed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Judges would the Chief Justice direct to hear your proceeding?
      `the number of Judges it would otherwise be heard before` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Judges would it otherwise be heard before (one, unless a written law provides another number)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(1A), may the Chief Justice direct this number of Judges` IS
    `s 10(1A) the Chief Justice may direct that the proceeding be heard before this number of Judges` `the number of Judges directed` `the number of Judges it would otherwise be heard before`

-- s 10(2). A Judge may exercise the jurisdiction of the General Division in any cause, matter or proceeding that a single Judge could have heard before 9 January 1970, or that the Rules direct or authorise a Judge to hear.
@export Under section 10(2), may a single Judge exercise the General Division's jurisdiction in my case?
GIVEN `a single Judge could have heard it immediately before 9 January 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could a single Judge have heard this kind of cause, matter or proceeding immediately before 9 January 1970?
      `the Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules direct or authorise it to be heard by a Judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules direct or authorise it to be heard by a Judge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(2), may a single Judge hear my case` IS
    `s 10(2) a Judge may exercise the jurisdiction of the General Division in the cause, matter or proceeding` `a single Judge could have heard it immediately before 9 January 1970` `the Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules direct or authorise it to be heard by a Judge`

-- s 10A(1). The General Division, the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal may, if they think fit, summon assessors to sit with them.
@export Under section 10A, may the court hearing my case summon assessors to sit with it?
GIVEN `the court hearing my case` IS A Court @desc Which court is hearing the case?
      `the court thinks fit to summon assessors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court think it fit to summon assessors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10A, may the court summon assessors` IS
    `s 10A the court may summon assessors` `the court hearing my case` `the court thinks fit to summon assessors`

-- s 10A(4). A party may take objection to a proposed assessor, on the person or on the person's qualification, in the prescribed manner.
@export Under section 10A(4), may I take objection to the person proposed as an assessor?
GIVEN `a person is proposed to be summoned as an assessor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a person proposed to be summoned as an assessor?
      `my objection is to the person or to the person's qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your objection to the person, or to the person's qualification?
      `I object in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you object in the manner the Rules prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10A(4), may I object to the proposed assessor` IS
    `s 10A(4) a party may take objection to the proposed assessor` `a person is proposed to be summoned as an assessor` `my objection is to the person or to the person's qualification` `I object in the prescribed manner`

-- s 10B(1). Subject to s 10B(2), the General Division is to sit on every day of the year except Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays.
@export Under section 10B(1), is the General Division to sit on this day?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking whether the General Division is to sit?
      `that day is a public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that day a public holiday?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10B(1), is the General Division to sit on the day` IS
    `s 10B(1) the General Division is to sit on the day` `the day I am asking about` (IF `that day is a public holiday` THEN LIST `the day I am asking about` ELSE EMPTY)

-- s 10B(2). A Judge may lawfully sit on a Saturday, Sunday, public holiday or day in a prescribed vacation if the Chief Justice directs it, or the Judge's opinion is that the business is extremely urgent.
@export Under section 10B(2), may a Judge lawfully sit on this day?
GIVEN `the day is a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday or falls in a vacation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, or in a vacation prescribed under section 7?
      `the Chief Justice has directed the Judge to sit on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Chief Justice directed the Judge to sit on that day or during that vacation?
      `in the Judge's opinion the business is extremely urgent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Judge's opinion, is the business to be despatched extremely urgent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10B(2), may a Judge lawfully sit on the day` IS
    `s 10B(2) the Judge may lawfully sit on the day` `the day is a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday or falls in a vacation` `the Chief Justice has directed the Judge to sit on that day` `in the Judge's opinion the business is extremely urgent`

-- s 13. A judgment for the payment of money may be enforced against all the judgment debtor's property by an enforcement order for seizure and sale, except the property described in paragraphs (a) to (e):
-- (a) wearing apparel, bedding and tools of trade, only while their value does not exceed $1,000; (b) tools of artisans, an agriculturist's implements of husbandry, and the animals, seed-grain or produce the court thinks necessary for a livelihood;
-- (c) wages or salary; (d) a Government pension, gratuity or allowance; (e) a partner's share, where the creditor may obtain a charge under a written law.
@export Under section 13, can the judgment debtor's property be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale?
GIVEN `the judgment is for the payment of money to any person or into court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment for the payment of money to any person or into court?
      `the kind of property` IS A `s 13 property` @desc What kind of property is it?
      `the value of the apparel, bedding, tools and implements, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is wearing apparel, bedding or tools of trade: what is its value, in dollars?
      `in the opinion of the court the animals, seed-grain or produce are necessary to earn the livelihood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an agriculturist's animals, seed-grain or produce: in the opinion of the court, are they necessary to earn a livelihood?
      `the judgment creditor is entitled to proceed to obtain a charge on the share under a written law relating to partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a share in a partnership: is the judgment creditor entitled to proceed to obtain a charge on the share under a written law relating to partnership?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 13, can the judgment debtor's property be seized` IS
    `s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` `the judgment is for the payment of money to any person or into court` `the kind of property` `the value of the apparel, bedding, tools and implements, in dollars` `in the opinion of the court the animals, seed-grain or produce are necessary to earn the livelihood` `the judgment creditor is entitled to proceed to obtain a charge on the share under a written law relating to partnership`

-- s 14(1). Only if a judgment or order is for the execution of a deed, the signing of a document or the indorsement of a negotiable instrument, and the party ordered is absent or neglects or refuses to do it, may the interested party prepare the instrument and tender it to the court for execution.
@export Under section 14(1), may I prepare the instrument and tender it to the court for execution?
GIVEN `the judgment or order is for the execution of a deed, the signing of a document or the indorsement of a negotiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment or order for the execution of a deed, the signing of a document or the indorsement of a negotiable instrument?
      `the party ordered is absent, or neglects or refuses to do it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the party ordered absent, or does the party neglect or refuse to do it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 14(1), may I prepare the instrument and tender it for execution` IS
    `s 14(1) the interested party may prepare the instrument and tender it to the court for execution` `the judgment or order is for the execution of a deed, the signing of a document or the indorsement of a negotiable instrument` `the party ordered is absent, or neglects or refuses to do it`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Does the High Court have jurisdiction over my case? (ss 16, 17, 17A)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 16(1). The General Division has jurisdiction to hear and try any action in personam where the defendant is served (in Singapore, or outside it as the Rules authorise), or submits to its jurisdiction.
@export Under section 16(1), does the General Division have jurisdiction to hear and try my action in personam?
GIVEN `my action is an action in personam` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your action an action in personam (against a person, rather than against property)?
      `the defendant is served in Singapore in the manner the Rules prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant served with the originating claim or other originating process in Singapore, in the manner prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules?
      `the defendant is served outside Singapore as the Rules authorise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant served outside Singapore, in the circumstances authorised by and in the manner prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules?
      `the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the defendant submit to the jurisdiction of the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 16(1), does the General Division have jurisdiction over my action in personam` IS
    `s 16(1) the General Division has jurisdiction to hear and try the action in personam` `my action is an action in personam` `the defendant is served in Singapore in the manner the Rules prescribe` `the defendant is served outside Singapore as the Rules authorise` `the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of the General Division`

-- s 17(1). The civil jurisdiction of the General Division includes divorce and matrimonial causes, admiralty, bankruptcy and company matters, guardianship, probate, a mediated settlement agreement to be recorded, and an international settlement agreement.
@export Under section 17(1), does the civil jurisdiction of the General Division include my kind of case?
GIVEN `what my case is about` IS A `Subject of the case` @desc What is your case about: divorce, admiralty or shipping, bankruptcy, companies, guardianship of infants, guardianship of persons of unsound mind, probate or administration, recording a mediated settlement agreement, an international settlement agreement, or something else?
      `no proceedings have been commenced in a court for the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you want a mediated settlement agreement recorded: have no proceedings been commenced in a court for the dispute?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 17(1), does the General Division's civil jurisdiction include my kind of case` IS
    `s 17(1) the civil jurisdiction of the General Division includes the subject` `what my case is about` `no proceedings have been commenced in a court for the dispute`

-- s 17A(1). Despite sections 16 and 17, the General Division has NO jurisdiction over matters within the Syariah Court's jurisdiction under s 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966, where all the parties are Muslims or were married under the Muslim law.
@export Under section 17A(1), is my case outside the General Division's jurisdiction because the Syariah Court has it?
GIVEN `the matters are within the Syariah Court's jurisdiction under section 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the matters come within the jurisdiction of the Syariah Court under section 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966?
      `all the parties are Muslims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the parties Muslims?
      `the parties were married under the Muslim law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the parties married under the provisions of the Muslim law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 17A(1), does the General Division have no jurisdiction over my case` IS
    `s 17A(1) the General Division has no jurisdiction to hear and try the civil proceedings` `the matters are within the Syariah Court's jurisdiction under section 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966` `all the parties are Muslims` `the parties were married under the Muslim law`

-- s 17A(3). Where civil proceedings involving custody or the division of property on divorce are between Muslims (or people married under the Muslim law), the General Division is to stay them if a Syariah Court divorce event
-- precedes or coincides with them (unless a commencement certificate has been filed), or custody proceedings if one follows them (unless a continuation certificate has been filed). Proceedings commenced or continued by consent with attendance certificates filed are excepted.
@export Under section 17A(3), is the General Division to stay my civil proceedings?
GIVEN `what my proceedings are about` IS A `Subject of the case` @desc What are your civil proceedings about: custody of a child, the disposition or division of property on divorce, maintenance for a wife or child, or something else?
      `all the parties are Muslims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the parties Muslims?
      `the parties were married under the Muslim law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the parties married under the provisions of the Muslim law?
      `the date my civil proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date were your civil proceedings commenced in the General Division?
      `divorce proceedings have been commenced in the Syariah Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have divorce proceedings been commenced in the Syariah Court?
      `the date they were commenced in the Syariah Court` IS A DATE @desc If divorce proceedings have been commenced in the Syariah Court: on what date?
      `a decree or order for divorce has been made by the Syariah Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Syariah Court made a decree or order for divorce?
      `the date the decree or order was made` IS A DATE @desc If the Syariah Court made a decree or order for divorce: on what date?
      `a divorce has been registered under section 102 of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a divorce been registered under section 102 of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966?
      `the date the divorce was registered` IS A DATE @desc If a divorce has been registered: on what date?
      `a Syariah Court commencement certificate has been filed with the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a Syariah Court commencement certificate been filed with the General Division?
      `a Syariah Court continuation certificate has been filed with the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a Syariah Court continuation certificate been filed with the General Division?
      `my proceedings were commenced by consent with the certificates of attendance filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were your proceedings commenced by consent of the parties, with the certificates of attendance filed?
      `my proceedings were continued by consent with the certificates of attendance filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were your proceedings continued by consent of the parties, with the certificates of attendance filed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 17A(3), is the General Division to stay my civil proceedings` IS
    `s 17A(3) the General Division is to stay the civil proceedings`
        (`s 17A civil proceedings` OF `what my proceedings are about`, `all the parties are Muslims`, `the parties were married under the Muslim law`, `the date my civil proceedings were commenced`,
            (`scja1 seat the date if it has happened` `divorce proceedings have been commenced in the Syariah Court` `the date they were commenced in the Syariah Court`),
            (`scja1 seat the date if it has happened` `a decree or order for divorce has been made by the Syariah Court` `the date the decree or order was made`),
            (`scja1 seat the date if it has happened` `a divorce has been registered under section 102 of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966` `the date the divorce was registered`),
            `a Syariah Court commencement certificate has been filed with the General Division`, `a Syariah Court continuation certificate has been filed with the General Division`,
            `my proceedings were commenced by consent with the certificates of attendance filed`, `my proceedings were continued by consent with the certificates of attendance filed`)

-- ss 16, 17, 17A(1) and 17A(2) together, gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B; fork F9): each section's own answer is computed by its layer-1 rule and passed to the gathering rule.
@export Under sections 16, 17 and 17A together, does the General Division have civil jurisdiction over my case?
GIVEN `my action is an action in personam` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your action an action in personam (against a person, rather than against property)?
      `the defendant is served in Singapore in the manner the Rules prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant served with the originating claim or other originating process in Singapore, in the manner prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules?
      `the defendant is served outside Singapore as the Rules authorise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant served outside Singapore, in the circumstances authorised by and in the manner prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules?
      `the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the defendant submit to the jurisdiction of the General Division?
      `another written law vests the jurisdiction in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another written law vest the jurisdiction in the General Division?
      `what my case is about` IS A `Subject of the case` @desc What is your case about: divorce, admiralty or shipping, bankruptcy, companies, guardianship, probate or administration, recording a mediated settlement agreement, an international settlement agreement, maintenance, custody, property on divorce, or something else?
      `no proceedings have been commenced in a court for the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you want a mediated settlement agreement recorded: have no proceedings been commenced in a court for the dispute?
      `the matters are within the Syariah Court's jurisdiction under section 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the matters come within the jurisdiction of the Syariah Court under section 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966?
      `the matters are within the Syariah Court's jurisdiction under section 35(2)(d) or (e), 51 or 52(3)(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the matters come within the jurisdiction of the Syariah Court under section 35(2)(d) or (e), 51 or 52(3)(c) or (d) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966?
      `all the parties are Muslims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the parties Muslims?
      `the parties were married under the Muslim law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the parties married under the provisions of the Muslim law?
      `a written law vests the jurisdiction in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For maintenance, custody or property on divorce: does a written law vest the jurisdiction to hear the proceeding in the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under sections 16, 17 and 17A together, does the General Division have civil jurisdiction over my case` IS
    `ss 16, 17 and 17A the General Division has civil jurisdiction by one of these sections`
        (`s 16(1) the General Division has jurisdiction to hear and try the action in personam` `my action is an action in personam` `the defendant is served in Singapore in the manner the Rules prescribe` `the defendant is served outside Singapore as the Rules authorise` `the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of the General Division`)
        (`s 16(2) the General Division has the jurisdiction vested in it by another written law` `another written law vests the jurisdiction in the General Division`)
        (`s 17(1) the civil jurisdiction of the General Division includes the subject` `what my case is about` `no proceedings have been commenced in a court for the dispute`)
        (`s 17A(1) the General Division has no jurisdiction to hear and try the civil proceedings` `the matters are within the Syariah Court's jurisdiction under section 35(2)(a), (b) or (c) of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966` `all the parties are Muslims` `the parties were married under the Muslim law`)
        (`s 17A(2) the General Division has the jurisdiction vested in it by written law over the civil proceedings` `what my case is about` `the matters are within the Syariah Court's jurisdiction under section 35(2)(d) or (e), 51 or 52(3)(c) or (d)` `a written law vests the jurisdiction in the General Division`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Can the court decide without a hearing, or dismiss an appeal summarily? (ss 17B, 17C)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 17B(1). The General Division may decide any matter in its original civil jurisdiction without hearing oral arguments, other than a matter prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules.
@export Under section 17B(1), may the General Division decide my matter without hearing oral arguments?
GIVEN `my matter is in the original civil jurisdiction of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your matter within the General Division's original civil jurisdiction?
      `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules prescribe as needing oral arguments?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 17B(1), may the General Division decide my matter without hearing oral arguments` IS
    `s 17B(1) the General Division may decide the matter without hearing oral arguments` `my matter is in the original civil jurisdiction of the General Division` `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules`

-- s 17B(2). Section 17B(1) does not allow any part of a proceeding where oral evidence is given to be conducted without an oral hearing, unless all the parties consent.
@export Under section 17B(2), does section 17B(1) allow a part of my proceeding where oral evidence is given to be conducted without an oral hearing?
GIVEN `oral evidence is given in this part of the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is oral evidence given in this part of the proceeding?
      `all the parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the parties consent to it being conducted without an oral hearing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 17B(2), does section 17B(1) allow this part to be conducted without an oral hearing` IS
    `s 17B(2) section 17B(1) allows this part of the proceeding to be conducted without an oral hearing` (`scja1 seat my hearing from what I know` `without hearing oral arguments` `oral evidence is given in this part of the hearing` `all the parties consent`)

-- s 17B(3). In any matter the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments, it may direct that the matter be heard asynchronously by exchange of written correspondence.
@export Under section 17B(3), may the General Division direct that my matter be heard by exchange of written correspondence?
GIVEN `my matter is one the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your matter one that the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 17B(3), may the General Division direct a written-correspondence hearing` IS
    `s 17B(3) the General Division may direct that the matter be heard in an asynchronous manner by exchange of written correspondence` `my matter is one the General Division may decide without hearing oral arguments`

-- s 17B(4). The General Division must not hear a matter asynchronously if that would be inconsistent with its duty to ensure the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties.
@export Under section 17B(4), must the General Division not hear my matter by exchange of written correspondence?
GIVEN `to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would hearing the matter by exchange of written correspondence be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 17B(4), must the General Division not hear my matter asynchronously` IS
    `s 17B(4) the General Division must not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` `to do so would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly to all parties`

-- s 17C(1). A Judge sitting in the General Division may, on his or her own motion, summarily dismiss an appeal against a decision of the Registrar relating to civil proceedings, if satisfied that every issue was already decided
-- in an earlier matter in which the appellant was involved, or that the conditions the Rules prescribe are met.
@export Under section 17C(1), may a Judge on his or her own motion summarily dismiss my appeal against the Registrar's decision?
GIVEN `my appeal is against a decision of the Registrar relating to civil proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal made against a decision of the Registrar relating to civil proceedings?
      `every issue in the appeal has already been decided in an earlier matter in which I was involved, so the appeal has no merit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Judge satisfied that every issue in the appeal has already been decided by the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal in an earlier matter in which the appellant was involved, and that the appeal therefore has no merit?
      `the conditions the Rules prescribe are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Judge satisfied that the conditions prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules are met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 17C(1), may a Judge summarily dismiss my appeal from the Registrar` IS
    `s 17C(1) a Judge sitting in the General Division may on his or her own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` `my appeal is against a decision of the Registrar relating to civil proceedings` `every issue in the appeal has already been decided in an earlier matter in which I was involved, so the appeal has no merit` `the conditions the Rules prescribe are met`

-- s 17C(2). Before summarily dismissing an appeal, the Judge must give the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause and consider the appellant's representations.
@export Under section 17C(2), can the Judge summarily dismiss my appeal now?
GIVEN `I was given a reasonable opportunity to show cause why the appeal should not be summarily dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given a reasonable opportunity to show cause why your appeal should not be summarily dismissed?
      `the Judge considered my representations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Judge consider your representations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 17C(2), can the Judge summarily dismiss my appeal now` IS
    `s 17C(2) the Judge may summarily dismiss the appeal under section 17C(1) now, as the section requires` `I was given a reasonable opportunity to show cause why the appeal should not be summarily dismissed` `the Judge considered my representations`

