@export Under section 73D(3)(b), must the other party be heard on the merits of my action or application before it is treated as struck out or dismissed?
GIVEN `my action or application is treated as struck out or dismissed` IS A `scja3 My answer` @desc Is your action or application one that section 73D(3) treats as struck out or dismissed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73D(3)(b), must the other party be heard on the merits of my action or application before it is treated as struck out or dismissed` IS
    `s 73D(3)(b) any other party must be heard on the merits of the action or application` (`scja3 what I say, as a fact` `my action or application is treated as struck out or dismissed`)

-- section 73D(4)(a).
@export Under section 73D(4)(a), is the period specified in the general civil restraint order within the 2-year limit?
GIVEN `the day the order takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the order take effect?
      `the day the order is to stop having effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the order to stop having effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73D(4)(a), is the period specified in the general civil restraint order within the 2-year limit` IS
    `s 73D(4)(a) the period specified in the order is within the limit` `the day the order takes effect` `the day the order is to stop having effect`

-- section 73D(4)(b).
@export Under section 73D(4)(b), does the general civil restraint order specify every court in which I am restrained as the section requires?
GIVEN `the order specifies every court or subordinate court in which the party is restrained from commencing any action or making any application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order specify every court or subordinate court in which you are restrained from commencing any action or making any application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73D(4)(b), does the general civil restraint order specify every court in which I am restrained as the section requires` IS
    `s 73D(4)(b) the order specifies every court or subordinate court in which the party is restrained, as the section requires` `the order specifies every court or subordinate court in which the party is restrained from commencing any action or making any application`

-- section 73D(5)(a).
@export Under section 73D(5)(a), may the court extend the period for which the general civil restraint order remains in effect?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `scja3 Which court` @desc Which court made the order?
      `the order is a general civil restraint order in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the general civil restraint order in effect?
      `the court considers it appropriate to extend the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court consider it appropriate to extend the period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73D(5)(a), may the court extend the period for which the general civil restraint order remains in effect` IS
    `s 73D(5)(a) the court may extend the period for which the order remains in effect` (`scja3 my court` `the court`) `the order is a general civil restraint order in effect` `the court considers it appropriate to extend the period`

-- section 73D(5).
@export Under section 73D(5), is the extension of the general civil restraint order within the 2-year limit?
GIVEN `the day the period ends before the extension` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period end before the extension?
      `the day the period is to end after the extension` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the period to end after the extension?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73D(5), is the extension of the general civil restraint order within the 2-year limit` IS
    `s 73D(5)(b) the extension is within the limit` `the day the period ends before the extension` `the day the period is to end after the extension`

-- section 73D(6) and (7).
@export Under section 73D(6) and (7), to which court must I apply for permission to appeal against the refusal of permission?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `scja3 Which court` @desc Which court made the general civil restraint order?
      `the court refused my application for permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court refuse your application for permission under section 73D(2)?
      `the court I appeal to` IS A `scja3 Which appeal court` @desc Under section 29C, to which court is your appeal to be made?
GIVETH A MAYBE Court
DECIDE `Under section 73D(6) and (7), to which court must I apply for permission to appeal against the refusal of permission` IS
    `s 73D(6) and (7) the court whose permission is needed to appeal against the refusal` (`scja3 my court` `the court`) `the court refused my application for permission` (`scja3 the court I appeal to` `the court I appeal to`)

-- section 74(1).
@export Under section 74(1), can the General Division order that I may not start or continue legal proceedings without its permission?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `scja3 Which court` @desc Which court is being asked to make the order?
      `the Attorney-General applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney-General applied for the order?
      `the General Division is satisfied that I have habitually and persistently and without any reasonable ground instituted vexatious legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division satisfied that you have habitually and persistently and without any reasonable ground instituted vexatious legal proceedings in any court or subordinate court?
      `I have been heard or given an opportunity of being heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been heard, or given an opportunity of being heard?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(1), can the General Division order that I may not start or continue legal proceedings without its permission` IS
    `s 74(1) the General Division may order that the person institute and continue legal proceedings only with its permission` (`scja3 my court` `the court`) `the Attorney-General applies` `the General Division is satisfied that I have habitually and persistently and without any reasonable ground instituted vexatious legal proceedings` `I have been heard or given an opportunity of being heard`

-- section 74(1)(a).
@export Under section 74(1)(a), may I start legal proceedings in a court or subordinate court?
GIVEN `the General Division has made an order against me under section 74(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division made an order against you under section 74(1)?
      `I have the permission of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the permission of the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(1)(a), may I start legal proceedings in a court or subordinate court` IS
    `s 74(1)(a) the person may institute legal proceedings in a court or subordinate court` `the General Division has made an order against me under section 74(1)` `I have the permission of the General Division`

-- section 74(1)(a).
@export Under section 74(1)(a), am I barred from starting legal proceedings in a court or subordinate court without permission?
GIVEN `the General Division has made an order against me under section 74(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division made an order against you under section 74(1)?
      `I have the permission of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the permission of the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(1)(a), am I barred from starting legal proceedings in a court or subordinate court without permission` IS
    `s 74(1)(a) the bar on instituting legal proceedings in a court or subordinate court applies` `the General Division has made an order against me under section 74(1)` `I have the permission of the General Division`

-- section 74(1)(b).
@export Under section 74(1)(b), may I continue the legal proceedings I started before the order?
GIVEN `the General Division has made an order against me under section 74(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division made an order against you under section 74(1)?
      `I started the legal proceedings before the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you start the legal proceedings before the order was made?
      `I have the permission of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the permission of the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(1)(b), may I continue the legal proceedings I started before the order` IS
    `s 74(1)(b) the person may continue the legal proceedings instituted before the order` `the General Division has made an order against me under section 74(1)` `I started the legal proceedings before the order was made` `I have the permission of the General Division`

-- section 74(1)(b).
@export Under section 74(1)(b), am I barred from continuing the legal proceedings I started before the order without permission?
GIVEN `the General Division has made an order against me under section 74(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division made an order against you under section 74(1)?
      `I started the legal proceedings before the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you start the legal proceedings before the order was made?
      `I have the permission of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the permission of the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(1)(b), am I barred from continuing the legal proceedings I started before the order without permission` IS
    `s 74(1)(b) the bar on continuing the legal proceedings instituted before the order applies` `the General Division has made an order against me under section 74(1)` `I started the legal proceedings before the order was made` `I have the permission of the General Division`

-- section 74(1)(b).
@export Under section 74(1)(b), may the General Division give me permission to continue the legal proceedings?
GIVEN `the General Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court?
      `the General Division is satisfied that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division satisfied that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(1)(b), may the General Division give me permission to continue the legal proceedings` IS
    `s 74(1)(b) the General Division may give permission to continue the legal proceedings` `the General Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court` `the General Division is satisfied that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings`

-- section 74(1)(b).
@export Under section 74(1)(b), is the General Division barred from giving me permission to continue the legal proceedings?
GIVEN `the General Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court?
      `the General Division is satisfied that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the General Division satisfied that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(1)(b), is the General Division barred from giving me permission to continue the legal proceedings` IS
    `s 74(1)(b) the bar on giving permission to continue the legal proceedings applies` `the General Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court` `the General Division is satisfied that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings`

-- section 74(2).
@export Under section 74(2), is the General Division to assign me an advocate and solicitor?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `scja3 Which court` @desc Which court is dealing with the application for the order?
      `an order against me is sought under section 74(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an order against you sought under section 74(1)?
      `I satisfy the General Division that I lack the means to retain an advocate and solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you satisfied the General Division that you lack the means to retain an advocate and solicitor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(2), is the General Division to assign me an advocate and solicitor` IS
    `s 74(2) the General Division is to assign an advocate and solicitor to the person` (`scja3 my court` `the court`) `an order against me is sought under section 74(1)` `I satisfy the General Division that I lack the means to retain an advocate and solicitor`

-- section 74(2A).
@export Under section 74(2A), to which court must I apply for permission to appeal against the order?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `scja3 Which court` @desc Which court made the order?
      `the order is an order made under section 74(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order an order made under section 74(1)?
      `the court I appeal to` IS A `scja3 Which appeal court` @desc Under section 29C, to which court is your appeal to be made?
GIVETH A MAYBE Court
DECIDE `Under section 74(2A), to which court must I apply for permission to appeal against the order` IS
    `s 74(2A) the court whose permission is needed to appeal against the order` (`scja3 my court` `the court`) `the order is an order made under section 74(1)` (`scja3 the court I appeal to` `the court I appeal to`)

-- section 74(2A).
@export Under section 74(2A), can I appeal against the order without permission?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `scja3 Which court` @desc Which court made the order?
      `the order is an order made under section 74(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order an order made under section 74(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(2A), can I appeal against the order without permission` IS
    `s 74(2A) the person may appeal against the order without permission` (`scja3 my court` `the court`) `the order is an order made under section 74(1)`

-- section 74(3).
@export Under section 74(3), can I appeal from an order refusing me permission to start or continue legal proceedings?
GIVEN `the order refuses permission under section 74(1) for the institution or continuance of legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order one refusing you permission, under section 74(1), to start or to continue legal proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(3), can I appeal from an order refusing me permission to start or continue legal proceedings` IS
    `s 74(3) an appeal lies from the order refusing permission` `the order refuses permission under section 74(1) for the institution or continuance of legal proceedings`


