§§ `Officers of the Supreme Court (ss 76 to 79)`
-- Situation: asked only of a person whose case, sale or complaint involves the Registrar or another officer of the Supreme Court.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- section 76.
@export Under section 76, may the Registrar investigate or hear and determine the proceedings I am in?
GIVEN `the officer` IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court` @desc Which officer of the Supreme Court is it?
      `the officer is a party to or personally interested in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer a party to, or personally interested in, the proceedings?
      `the Chief Justice has approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Chief Justice approved?
      `the parties have consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties consented?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76, may the Registrar investigate or hear and determine the proceedings I am in` IS
    `s 76 the officer may investigate or hear and determine the proceedings` `the officer` `the officer is a party to or personally interested in the proceedings` `the Chief Justice has approved` `the parties have consented`

-- section 77.
@export Under section 77, may an officer who has a duty in the sale of property buy or bid for it?
GIVEN `the officer has a duty to perform in connection with the sale of the property under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the officer have a duty to perform in connection with the sale of the property under a written law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77, may an officer who has a duty in the sale of property buy or bid for it` IS
    `s 77 the officer may purchase or bid for the property` `the officer has a duty to perform in connection with the sale of the property under a written law`

-- section 78(1).
@export Under section 78(1), may the Registrar inquire in a summary way into a charge I make against an officer?
GIVEN `the officer is charged with extortion or misconduct while acting under colour of the process of the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer charged with extortion or misconduct while acting under colour of the process of the Supreme Court?
      `the officer is charged with not duly paying or accounting for money levied under the authority of this Act or Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer charged with not duly paying or accounting for money levied under the authority of this Act or Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(1), may the Registrar inquire in a summary way into a charge I make against an officer` IS
    `s 78(1) it is lawful for the Registrar to inquire into the matter in a summary way` `the officer is charged with extortion or misconduct while acting under colour of the process of the Supreme Court` `the officer is charged with not duly paying or accounting for money levied under the authority of this Act or Rules of Court`

-- section 78(3).
@export Under section 78(3), may the Registrar order repayment of what was extorted, and damages and costs?
GIVEN `the Registrar is conducting an inquiry under section 78(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar conducting an inquiry under section 78(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(3), may the Registrar order repayment of what was extorted, and damages and costs` IS
    `s 78(3) the Registrar may order repayment of the money extorted, due payment of the money levied, and payment of damages and costs` `the Registrar is conducting an inquiry under section 78(1)`

-- section 78(5).
@export Under section 78(5), can I appeal to the Chief Justice from the Registrar's order?
GIVEN `the order was made by the Registrar under section 78` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order made by the Registrar under section 78?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(5), can I appeal to the Chief Justice from the Registrar's order` IS
    `s 78(5) an appeal lies to the Chief Justice` `the order was made by the Registrar under section 78`

-- section 78(6).
@export Under section 78(6), can I appeal from the Chief Justice's decision?
GIVEN `the decision is the Chief Justice's decision on an appeal under section 78(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision the Chief Justice's decision on an appeal under section 78(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(6), can I appeal from the Chief Justice's decision` IS
    `s 78(6) a further appeal lies from the decision of the Chief Justice` `the decision is the Chief Justice's decision on an appeal under section 78(5)`

-- section 79(1).
@export Under section 79(1), is the Registrar, or another person acting judicially, not liable to be sued by me for what they did in the discharge of their judicial duty?
GIVEN `the person is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or another person acting judicially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or another person acting judicially?
      `the act was done in the discharge of the person's judicial duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done in the discharge of the person's judicial duty?
      `the person at the time in good faith believed himself or herself to have jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time, did the person in good faith believe himself or herself to have jurisdiction to do or order the act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(1), is the Registrar, or another person acting judicially, not liable to be sued by me for what they did in the discharge of their judicial duty` IS
    `s 79(1) the person is not liable to be sued in a court exercising civil jurisdiction for the act` `the person is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or another person acting judicially` `the act was done in the discharge of the person's judicial duty` `the person at the time in good faith believed himself or herself to have jurisdiction`

-- section 79(2).
@export Under section 79(2), is an officer charged with executing the court's process not liable to be sued?
GIVEN `the officer is charged with the duty of executing a writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other mandatory process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer an officer of the Supreme Court charged with the duty of executing a writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other mandatory process of the court?
      `the claim is for the execution of the process, or for damage to property in effecting it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim for the execution of, or an attempt to execute, the process, or for damage to property in effecting or attempting to effect execution?
      `it appears that the officer knowingly acted in excess of the authority conferred by the process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear that the officer knowingly acted in excess of the authority conferred by the process?
      `the only ground for saying so is a dispute as to the ownership of property seized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only ground for saying that the officer acted knowingly in excess of authority a dispute as to the ownership of property seized under an enforcement order or writ of distress?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(2), is an officer charged with executing the court's process not liable to be sued` IS
    `s 79(2) the officer is not liable to be sued` `the officer is charged with the duty of executing a writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other mandatory process of the court` `the claim is for the execution of the process, or for damage to property in effecting it` `it appears that the officer knowingly acted in excess of the authority conferred by the process` `the only ground for saying so is a dispute as to the ownership of property seized`

-- section 79(4).
@export Under section 79(4), is a professional appointed to examine and assess a child or person not liable to be sued for the examination?
GIVEN `the professional was appointed by the General Division to examine and assess a child or person for expert evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the professional appointed by the General Division to examine and assess a child or person for the purposes of preparing expert evidence for use in proceedings involving the custody or welfare of the child or involving the person?
      `the act was done for the purposes of the examination or assessment, or the preparation of the expert evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done for the purposes of the examination or assessment, or the preparation of the expert evidence?
      `the act was done in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done in good faith?
      `the act involved fraud or wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act involve fraud or wilful misconduct on the professional's part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(4), is a professional appointed to examine and assess a child or person not liable to be sued for the examination` IS
    `s 79(4) the registered medical practitioner, psychologist, counsellor, social worker or mental health professional is not liable to be sued for the act` `the professional was appointed by the General Division to examine and assess a child or person for expert evidence` `the act was done for the purposes of the examination or assessment, or the preparation of the expert evidence` `the act was done in good faith` `the act involved fraud or wilful misconduct`

-- section 79(5).
@export Under section 79(5), is the Registrar or a court-appointed mediator not liable to be sued for an act done for a mediation?
GIVEN `the person is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a court-appointed mediator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a court-appointed mediator?
      `the act was done for the purposes of a mediation conducted by the person in the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done for the purposes of a mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process conducted by the person in the Supreme Court?
      `the act was done in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done in good faith?
      `the act involved fraud or wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act involve fraud or wilful misconduct on the person's part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(5), is the Registrar or a court-appointed mediator not liable to be sued for an act done for a mediation` IS
    `s 79(5) the person is not liable to be sued for the act done for the purposes of the mediation` `the person is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a court-appointed mediator` `the act was done for the purposes of a mediation conducted by the person in the Supreme Court` `the act was done in good faith` `the act involved fraud or wilful misconduct`

-- section 79(6).
@export Under section 79(6), am I immune from legal proceedings for something I did or did not do in compliance with a prerogative order?
GIVEN `the act or omission was in compliance with a prerogative order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act or omission in compliance with a prerogative order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(6), am I immune from legal proceedings for something I did or did not do in compliance with a prerogative order` IS
    `s 79(6) the person or entity is immune from legal proceedings in respect of the act or omission` `the act or omission was in compliance with a prerogative order`


