§§ `Interest and the conversion of pending proceedings (ss 80 and 82)`
-- Situation: asked only of a person with a debt that carries interest, or a petition, motion or originating motion pending when the law changed the way such matters are begun.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- section 80(2)(j).
@export Under section 80(2)(j), can the Rules of Court regulate the rate of interest on my debt at this rate?
GIVEN `the rate of interest per annum, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What rate of interest per annum, as a percentage, is in question?
      `the parties have otherwise agreed the rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and the other party otherwise agreed the rate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 80(2)(j), can the Rules of Court regulate the rate of interest on my debt at this rate` IS
    `s 80(2)(j) the Rules of Court may regulate the rate of interest at that rate` `the rate of interest per annum, as a percentage` `the parties have otherwise agreed the rate`

-- section 82(1).
@export Under section 82(1), may the court order that my pending petition, motion or originating motion be converted?
GIVEN `under a written law the action or application may be commenced in or made to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under a written law, may the civil action or application be commenced in or made to the Court of Appeal, a Judge of Appeal, the High Court, a Judge or the Registrar?
      `the law now requires a writ of summons, originating summons or summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the written law been amended to require a writ of summons, an originating summons or a summons instead of a petition, a motion or an originating motion?
      `mine was commenced or made before the amendment by petition, motion or originating motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your action or application commenced or made before the date of the amendment, by petition, motion or originating motion?
      `mine is still pending before the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it still pending before the court on or after that date?
      `the court thinks it just and expedient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court think it just and expedient?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 82(1), may the court order that my pending petition, motion or originating motion be converted` IS
    `s 82(1) the Court may order that the pending action or application be converted and continued` `under a written law the action or application may be commenced in or made to the court` `the law now requires a writ of summons, originating summons or summons` `mine was commenced or made before the amendment by petition, motion or originating motion` `mine is still pending before the court` `the court thinks it just and expedient`

-- section 82(3)(b).
@export Under section 82(3)(b), may the court give directions on the conduct and costs of my converted action or application?
GIVEN `my pending action or application has been converted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your pending action or application been converted under section 82(1) or (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 82(3)(b), may the court give directions on the conduct and costs of my converted action or application` IS
    `s 82(3)(b) the Court may give the parties directions as to the conduct and costs of the action or application` `my pending action or application has been converted`


