-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Appeals from a decision (Second to Tenth Schedules, as they bear on an appeal)`
-- Situation: asked only of a person who wishes to appeal, or to resist an appeal, and who has the decision in front of them. The form can ask "Do you wish to appeal a decision of a court?" before showing this group.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- schedule 3.
@export Under schedule 3, does my appeal against this decision of a District Court or Magistrate's Court need the permission of that court or the General Division?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `scja3 Which court` @desc Which court made the decision?
      `what the order was about` IS A `Subject of an order or application` @desc What was the order or application about?
      `how the order went` IS A `Way an order went` @desc How did the order go?
      `I am the party defending those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the party who is defending, and who must pay into court or give security for the sum claimed?
      `I am the party against whom the default judgment had been entered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the party against whom the default judgment had been entered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3, does my appeal against this decision of a District Court or Magistrate's Court need the permission of that court or the General Division` IS
    `sch 3 an appeal lies only with permission of that court or the General Division` (`scja3 my decision` (`scja3 my court` `the court`) `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` `any other civil matter` `what the order was about` `how the order went` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `I am the party defending those proceedings` `I am the party against whom the default judgment had been entered`

-- schedule 4.
@export Under schedule 4, is this decision of the General Division one that no appeal can be brought against?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `scja3 Which court` @desc Which court made the decision?
      `what the order was about` IS A `Subject of an order or application` @desc What was the order or application about?
      `how the order went` IS A `Way an order went` @desc How did the order go?
      `the order was made by consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the judgment or order made by consent of the parties?
      `the parties agreed in writing that the decision is final` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the parties agree in writing, signed by or on behalf of each party, that the decision is final?
      `what the decision was made in the exercise of` IS A `Jurisdiction exercised` @desc In the exercise of which jurisdiction was the decision made?
      `the decision was made after the trial of an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision a judgment given after the trial of an action (whether or not all the parties took part in the trial)?
      `a Judge made the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a Judge make the order?
      `permission to amend was applied for after a relevant period of limitation had expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was permission to amend applied for after a relevant period of limitation had expired?
      `the amendment corrects the name of a party or alters the capacity in which a party sues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment correct the name of a party or alter the capacity in which a party sues?
      `the amendment adds or substitutes a new cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment add or substitute a new cause of action?
      `the decision involves the exercise of the appellate civil jurisdiction mentioned in section 23 of the Family Justice Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision involve the exercise of the appellate civil jurisdiction mentioned in section 23 of the Family Justice Act 2014?
      `I prove that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prove that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality?
      `I prove a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prove a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice?
      `the agreement that the decision is final relates only to part of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement that the decision is final relate only to part of the decision?
      `my appeal is against the part the agreement relates to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against the part of the decision that the agreement relates to?
      `the action was ordered to be dealt with under an expedited procedure that restricts appeals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the action ordered, with the consent of all the parties, to be dealt with under an expedited procedure that restricts appeals?
      `the order refused a request for the expedited procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the order refuse a request, made with the consent of all the parties, for the expedited procedure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 4, is this decision of the General Division one that no appeal can be brought against` IS
    `sch 4 the Fourth Schedule says no appeal can be brought` (`scja3 my decision` (`scja3 my court` `the court`) `what the decision was made in the exercise of` `a civil proceeding` `any other civil matter` `what the order was about` `how the order went` `the order was made by consent` `the decision was made after the trial of an action` FALSE `the parties agreed in writing that the decision is final`) (`sch 4 facts about the decision` OF `a Judge made the order`, `permission to amend was applied for after a relevant period of limitation had expired`, `the amendment corrects the name of a party or alters the capacity in which a party sues`, `the amendment adds or substitutes a new cause of action`, `the decision involves the exercise of the appellate civil jurisdiction mentioned in section 23 of the Family Justice Act 2014`, `I prove that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality`, `I prove a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice`, `the agreement that the decision is final relates only to part of the decision`, `my appeal is against the part the agreement relates to`, `the action was ordered to be dealt with under an expedited procedure that restricts appeals`, `the order refused a request for the expedited procedure`)

-- schedule 5 paragraphs 3, 4(1) and 5(1).
@export Under schedule 5 paragraphs 3, 4(1) and 5(1), do I need permission of the appellate court to appeal against this decision of the General Division?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `scja3 Which court` @desc Which court made the decision?
      `what the order was about` IS A `Subject of an order or application` @desc What was the order or application about?
      `how the order went` IS A `Way an order went` @desc How did the order go?
      `the order was made by consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the judgment or order made by consent of the parties?
      `the parties agreed in writing that the decision is final` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the parties agree in writing, signed by or on behalf of each party, that the decision is final?
      `what the decision was made in the exercise of` IS A `Jurisdiction exercised` @desc In the exercise of which jurisdiction was the decision made?
      `a Judge made the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a Judge make the order?
      `I am the party on whom the condition of payment into court or security falls` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the party on whom the condition of payment into court or security falls?
      `permission to amend was applied for after a relevant period of limitation had expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was permission to amend applied for after a relevant period of limitation had expired?
      `the amendment corrects the name of a party or alters the capacity in which a party sues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment correct the name of a party or alter the capacity in which a party sues?
      `the amendment adds or substitutes a new cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment add or substitute a new cause of action?
      `the only issue in my appeal relates to costs or fees for hearing dates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the only issue in your appeal relate to costs or fees for hearing dates?
      `the Judge was sitting in chambers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the Judge sitting in chambers?
      `the Judge decided in a summary way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Judge decide in a summary way?
      `the facts are not in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the facts not in dispute?
